<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
  <!--
    App-wide compact control heights (field feedback: standard Button/ComboBox chrome
    reads too tall). Reference look is the "+ Material" button in the Fabrication Process
    editor (ProcessManagementWindow.axaml, FontSize="10" Padding="6,1") — but that button
    also shrinks FontSize, which is explicitly out of scope here (many buttons carry longer
    labels than "+ Material" and a global font shrink is a separate, riskier change).

    Approach: override the Fluent theme's resource keys that Button's and ComboBox's
    ControlThemes consume for sizing, instead of a Style Selector="Button"/"ComboBox".
    Reason: Avalonia's ToggleButton (and its subclasses CheckBox/RadioButton) derive from
    Button at the CLR level, so a type Selector="Button" Style would also match them.
    Scope of the keys (verified against Avalonia.Themes.Fluent 11.3.13): ButtonPadding is
    read not only by the plain Button ControlTheme but ALSO by ToggleButton and RepeatButton,
    so those render equally compact — accepted, the compact look is intended app-wide.
    CheckBox and RadioButton have their own keys (CheckBoxMinHeight/RadioButtonMinHeight, no
    "*Padding" key of their own) and are untouched by this override.

    Measured Fluent defaults (headless Skia, FontSize 14, dark theme) before this change:
      ButtonPadding            = 8,5,8,6   -> Button renders at 32px tall
      ComboBoxPadding           = 12,5,0,7  -> ComboBox renders at 32px tall (MinHeight=32)
      ComboBoxItemThemePadding  = 11,5,11,7 -> dropdown ComboBoxItem rows
    Button has no "ButtonMinHeight" resource — its height is purely padding+content driven,
    so it is not overridden here (there is nothing to hook).

    Target ~40% flatter (per field feedback) is bounded by the unchanged FontSize=14 content
    line height (~21px) — reducing vertical padding to the practical floor (without clipping
    text) lands Button/ComboBox at 24px (32 -> 24, a verified 25% reduction, no clipping).
    Hitting the full 40% would require also shrinking FontSize, which this change intentionally
    does not do (see PR notes for this trade-off).

    Follow-up (field test found 3 gaps — TextBox/NumericUpDown untouched, Flyout/Transient
    buttons still tall): verified against Avalonia.Themes.Fluent 11.3.13 source.
    TextBox's ControlTheme (Controls/TextBox.xaml) and NumericUpDown's ControlTheme
    (Controls/NumericUpDown.xaml) both read the SAME three keys for their outer control
    (NumericUpDown's inner PART_TextBox padding is a TemplateBinding to NumericUpDown's own
    Padding, so one override drives both controls):
      TextControlThemeMinHeight = 32   (Accents/BaseResources.xaml)
      TextControlThemeMinWidth  = 64   (unrelated to height — left untouched)
      TextControlThemePadding   = 10,6,6,5
    AutoCompleteBox (Controls/AutoCompleteBox.xaml) also reads TextControlThemePadding for
    its own Padding, and its inner PART_TextBox reads the same three keys again — both layers
    compact together, which is fine (no clipping: MinHeight is a floor, never a fixed Height).
    NumericUpDown's spinner RepeatButtons already render compact: their Padding is
    "{StaticResource ButtonPadding}" (Controls/ButtonSpinner.xaml), so they picked up the
    ButtonPadding override above for free; their height stretches to the ButtonSpinner's
    border, which now shrinks with TextControlThemeMinHeight.
  -->
  <Styles.Resources>
    <ResourceDictionary>
      <Thickness x:Key="ButtonPadding">8,1,8,2</Thickness>

      <!-- Left/right unchanged (12 left, 0 right — the 0 leaves room for the drop-down
           arrow glyph drawn by the ComboBox template); only vertical padding is reduced. -->
      <Thickness x:Key="ComboBoxPadding">12,1,0,2</Thickness>
      <Thickness x:Key="ComboBoxItemThemePadding">11,1,11,2</Thickness>
      <x:Double x:Key="ComboBoxMinHeight">21</x:Double>

      <!-- TextBox / NumericUpDown / AutoCompleteBox: same reduce-vertical-only pattern as
           Button/ComboBox above. Left=10/Right=6 unchanged (Right=6 leaves room for the
           clear/reveal-password glyph button some TextBoxes host in InnerRightContent);
           only Top/Bottom drop to the 1/2 floor. MinHeight 32 -> 21 matches ComboBoxMinHeight
           so text inputs and combo boxes align at the same row height. -->
      <Thickness x:Key="TextControlThemePadding">10,1,6,2</Thickness>
      <x:Double x:Key="TextControlThemeMinHeight">21</x:Double>
    </ResourceDictionary>
  </Styles.Resources>

  <!-- FontSize 12 (down from the Fluent 14) closes the gap to the requested ~40% flatter:
       with the reduced padding above, Button/ComboBox/TextBox/NumericUpDown land at ~21px
       (32 -> ~21). Type selectors match by StyleKey, so plain Button/ComboBox/TextBox/
       NumericUpDown are hit while CheckBox/ToggleButton/RadioButton (own StyleKeys and
       ControlThemes) stay untouched; views that set FontSize locally (most of the dense
       panels use 9-11 already) win anyway. -->
  <Style Selector="Button">
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="ComboBox">
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="TextBox">
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="NumericUpDown">
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12"/>
  </Style>
</Styles>
